      "description": "The immutable prelaunch binding records input_sha256 and recipe_sha256, but verify_settlement never checks either against the final HTTP run. verify_public_export compares exported bytes and metadata with that later HTTP run only. A shared projection drift can make both later observations agree on replacement input/recipe bytes while disagreeing with prepared execution evidence.",
      "witnesses": [
        "independent_lineage_projection_probe.py",
        "lineage-projection-results.json",
        "lineage-input-report.json",
        "lineage-recipe-report.json"
      ],
      "result": "Both full synthetic exercises return PASS with four attempts, 120 charges and two structurally valid exports. All four final run input hashes or recipe hashes differ from the prelaunch binding. A newline is appended only to exported inputs/recipes, and corresponding later HTTP/export hashes and recipe environment specifications are updated. Prelaunch bindings, requests, receipts, broker diagnostics and runtime source remain unchanged.",
      "limitation": "The existing synthetic fixture mocks provider, CLI initialization, Docker and checkpoint effects. This is a qualification-checker correlation gap, not evidence that production Store/export behavior normally changes these fields.",
      "fix": "Require final HTTP input_sha256 and recipe_sha256 to equal the retained prelaunch binding, and recipe/condition to equal the fixed matrix or captured prelaunch values, before accepting settlement. Preserve this comparison through the final oracle and exported projection. Add both shared-projection regressions."
    }
